<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss governnment extends mandates for SNB leaders.</title>
<headline>Swiss governnment extends mandates for SNB leaders.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss government has extended Swiss National National Bank (SNB) Chairman Hans Meyer's term in office by another six years, a government statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cabinet's decision keeps Meyer in his post during the period from July 1, 1997 to June 30, 2003.</p>
<p>Directorate members Jean-Pierre Roth and Bruno Gehrig were also reappointed, as were their deputies and directors of the central bank's branch offices.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
